[SOURCE 1: Attendance Module.docx]
Attendance Module Key Features:

Submit and manage individual and bulk attendance requests and corrections

Request exemptions for various attendance flags

Track project-based work hours via Work Sheets

Manage remote work and shift change requests

Finalize monthly attendance records via Attendance Close

Configure shift structures, penalty rules, and approval hierarchies

Attendance Module Business Value:

Streamlines attendance tracking and correction workflows

Reduces manual errors and administrative overhead

Ensures policy compliance and transparency in attendance management

Provides centralized reporting and audit trails for all attendance-related activities

Attendance Module Navigation Path:

Top Navigation → Attendance Module

Attendance Request

The Attendance Request form is the primary interface for employees and HR to manage attendance corrections and irregularities.

[SOURCE 2: Attendance Module (5.10).docx]
Employees can regularize missing entries or apply for attendance adjustments, while managers can review and approve these requests.

[SOURCE 3: Attendance Module.docx]
Attendance Request General:

Employees can view their own attendance records and request history.

[SOURCE 4: Attendance Module (5.10).docx]
Attendance Request

Employees can raise attendance requests by selecting employee, date, times, and reason; requests are submitted for approval.

⦁ Click Attendance on the top navigation bar.

⦁ Open the Attendance Request form.

⦁ Click Add New Request.

⦁ Select employee and attendance date.

⦁ Enter In & Out time, select attendance type, and enter reason.

⦁ Click Submit to raise a requisition.

[SOURCE 5: Attendance Module.docx]
Attendance Request View Report:

Apply filters (Date Range, Employee, Request Type, Status)

Click View Report to display or download request summaries

Standard Operating Procedures / Key Details

Request Types Supported:

Individual entries (e.g., missing punch, correction)

Multiple entries via Irregular Request (e.g., Missing, Absent)

Attendance Request Attachments:

Accepts PDF, DOC, DOCX, XLSX, JPG, JPEG, PNG formats.

[SOURCE 6: Attendance Module.docx]
Exemption Request

The Exemption Request form allows employees to request exemptions for specific attendance flags such as Late In, Half Day, Short Day, Absent for Short Time, Absent, and Missing Attendance. Exemption Request Navigation Path:

Attendance Module → Exemption Request

Exemption Request Process / Flow:

Click Attendance → Exemption Request.

